{"questions":[{"question_id":"1ky7ckz7x","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-13-elements-boron-family","type":"mcqm","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"the-correct-statements-for-orthoboric-acid-isare-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-bo5mtelgsqkgvfcb","content":"The correct statement(s) for orthoboric acid is/are","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"it behaves as a weak acid in water due to self ionisation"},{"identifier":"B","content":"acidity of its aqueous solution increases upon addition of ethylene glycol"},{"identifier":"C","content":"it has a three dimensional structure due to hydrogen bonding"},{"identifier":"D","content":"it is a weak electrolyte in water"}],"correct_options":["B","D"],"explanation":"(a) It does not undergo self ionisation in water but accepts an electron pair from water, so it behaves as weak monobasic acid<br><br>H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.032ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.195ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -514 1000 528\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21CC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-21CC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> B(OH)<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.432ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 633.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> + H<sup>+</sup><br><br>Hence, (a) is incorrect.<br><br>(b) When treated with 1, 2-dihydroxy or polyhydroxy compounds, they form chelate (ring complex) which effectively remove [B(OH)<sub>4</sub>]<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> species from solution and thereby produce maximum number of H<sub>3</sub>O<sup>+</sup> or H<sup>+</sup> ions, i.e., results in increased acidity.<br><br>(c) Baric acid crystallises in a layer structure in which planar triangular BO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.706ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.232ex\" height=\"2.701ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -881.8 986.7 1194\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(33,411.6) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-296.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ions are bonded together through hydrogen bonds.<br><br>(d) In water the pK<sub>a</sub> value of H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub> is 9.25<br><br>H<sub>3</sub>BO<sub>3</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.032ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.195ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -514 1000 528\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21CC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-21CC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> B(OH)<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.432ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 633.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> + H<sup>+</sup> ; pK<sub>a</sub> = 9.25<br><br>So, it is weak electrolyte in water."}]}